1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,927
BugReplay starts with a symptom and a URL.

2
00:00:02,927 --> 00:00:06,442
The cart sometimes disappears after an address change.

3
00:00:06,442 --> 00:00:10,653
The model gets browser observations, without a trigger recipe.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,887
This is the actual recorded investigation.

5
00:00:14,887 --> 00:00:22,394
Claude explores the controlled shop, adds items, changes checkout options, and checks the cart after saves.

6
00:00:22,394 --> 00:00:28,452
The runner records the full setup prefix, then compiles a Playwright test from trusted actions.

7
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:41,631
Confirmation comes from two fresh browser replays, without another model call.

8
00:00:41,631 --> 00:00:47,263
Both reach the intended cart preservation assertion: two items become an empty cart.

9
00:00:47,263 --> 00:00:54,969
The saved test, report, reproduction JSON, screenshots and original videos identify the same run.

10
00:00:56,503 --> 00:01:03,996
Neatlogs exposed a real failure: the provider returned prose with a JSON suffix, while the wrapper rejected it.

11
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:11,024
We added bounded format recovery and explicit disabled control observations.

12
00:01:11,024 --> 00:01:16,011
After the changes, one of three buggy investigations confirmed the defect.

13
00:01:16,011 --> 00:01:18,120
Two others did not reproduce it.

14
00:01:19,857 --> 00:01:22,442
Entire preserves the fix context.

15
00:01:22,442 --> 00:01:29,172
This is an authentic checkpoint metadata export for the actual engine change, linked to its commit and diff.

16
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:33,498
It records bounded continuation and disabled control visibility.

17
00:01:33,498 --> 00:01:37,156
CFO dot A I makes the pricing tradeoff visible.

18
00:01:37,156 --> 00:01:46,043
Our assumed forty nine dollar plan leaves twelve point nine three cents per run, after fees, at a seventy percent contribution target.

19
00:01:46,043 --> 00:01:50,486
This selected run alone has fifteen point six cents of gateway accounting.

20
00:01:50,486 --> 00:01:54,989
Failed attempts also count. Cash billing and credits remain unknown.

21
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:58,558
Now the same saved test runs against the corrected shop.

22
00:01:58,558 --> 00:02:04,552
Only the base URL changes. Its hash stays identical in a fresh browser context.

23
00:02:04,552 --> 00:02:08,837
Both cart items remain, and the preservation assertion passes.

24
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:16,096
This M V P covers one controlled shop and one defect class.

25
00:02:16,096 --> 00:02:18,193
Inspect the proof and its limits.
